@startuml
title Order Payment Flow

actor Client

participant "order-service" as OrderService
database "order DB" as OrderDb
participant "order outbox publisher" as OrderOutbox
queue "Kafka" as Kafka
participant "payment-service" as PaymentService
database "payment DB" as PaymentDb
participant "payment provider" as PaymentProvider

Client -> OrderService: POST /orders

OrderService -> OrderDb: save Order\n+ OutboxEvent(OrderCreated)
OrderDb --> OrderService: commit

OrderService --> Client: orderId + CREATED

OrderOutbox -> OrderDb: load unpublished events
OrderDb --> OrderOutbox: OrderCreated
OrderOutbox -> Kafka: publish OrderCreated

Kafka -> PaymentService: OrderCreated

PaymentService -> PaymentDb: check ProcessedEvent(eventId)

alt event already processed
    PaymentDb --> PaymentService: exists
    PaymentService --> Kafka: processing completed
else new event
    PaymentService -> PaymentDb: save Payment(CREATED)\n+ ProcessedEvent(eventId)
    PaymentDb --> PaymentService: commit
end

PaymentService -> PaymentProvider: charge(orderId, amount)

alt payment succeeded
    PaymentProvider --> PaymentService: SUCCESS

    PaymentService -> PaymentDb: Payment -> SUCCEEDED\n+ OutboxEvent(PaymentSucceeded)
    PaymentDb --> PaymentService: commit

    PaymentService -> Kafka: publish PaymentSucceeded
    Kafka -> OrderService: PaymentSucceeded

    OrderService -> OrderDb: Order -> CONFIRMED
    OrderDb --> OrderService: commit

else payment failed
    PaymentProvider --> PaymentService: FAILED(reason)

    PaymentService -> PaymentDb: Payment -> FAILED\n+ OutboxEvent(PaymentFailed)
    PaymentDb --> PaymentService: commit

    PaymentService -> Kafka: publish PaymentFailed
    Kafka -> OrderService: PaymentFailed

    OrderService -> OrderDb: Order -> CANCELED
    OrderDb --> OrderService: commit
end

note right of Kafka
Key learning points:

1. DB + Kafka is a dual-write problem
   -> Transactional Outbox

2. Kafka may redeliver messages
   -> Idempotent Consumer

3. Services become consistent over time
   -> Eventual Consistency

4. Later:
   Payment succeeded,
   Inventory failed
   -> Saga / Compensation
end note

@enduml